[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Understanding Shallow APIs in Vue.js (shallowRef, shallowReactive, shallowReadonly)"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"By default, Vue.js makes your state deeply reactive. When you mutate nested properties, Vue detects the changes and triggers UI updates. While convenient, this deep traversal can cause significant performance overhead when dealing with large datasets, third-party libraries, or immutable structures. Vue's Shallow APIs provide a way to opt out of this deep reactivity."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. shallowRef"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The shallowRef function is a shallow version of ref. It tracks reactivity only for the .value property itself, rather than recursively converting nested objects or arrays into reactive proxies."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"import { shallowRef } from 'vue';

const state = shallowRef({ count: 1 });

// Does NOT trigger UI updates
state.value.count = 2;

// DOES trigger UI updates
state.value = { count: 2 };"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. shallowReactive"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"While shallowRef controls reactivity at the .value level, shallowReactive applies to objects. Only root-level properties are reactive. Nested objects remain plain, unreactive JavaScript objects."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"import { shallowReactive } from 'vue';

const state = shallowReactive({
  user: 'Alice',
  settings: {
    theme: 'dark'
  }
});

// Triggers UI update
state.user = 'Bob';

// Does NOT trigger UI update
state.settings.theme = 'light';"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. shallowReadonly"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"The shallowReadonly API makes only the root-level properties immutable. Nested properties inside the object can still be mutated freely."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"import { shallowReadonly } from 'vue';

const state = shallowReadonly({
  config: {
    apiEndpoint: 'https://api.example.com'
  }
});

// Fails in development (warns mutation of readonly property)
state.config = {};

// Allowed (nested properties are not readonly)
state.config.apiEndpoint = 'https://api.newsite.com';"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Use Cases for Shallow APIs"},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Large data structures: Optimizing performance when rendering large read-only lists or datasets where deep observation is unnecessary."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Integration with external state managers: Holding instances of non-Vue libraries or complex classes inside a Vue component."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Immutability patterns: Forcing replacement-based state updates rather than mutation-based updates to improve predictability."}]
